<title>USA: United Dominion Realty sells building.</title>
<headline>United Dominion Realty sells building.</headline>
<dateline>RICHMOND, Va. 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Dominion Realty Trust Inc said Friday it has sold a 60,000 square foot industrial building in Roanoke to Precision Investment Corp for about $685,000.</p>
<p>As a result of the sale, the company wil post a gain of about $250,000 in this year's fourth quarter.</p>
<p>The company said the transaction was structured to qualify as a tax-deferred exchange which will result in the deferral of the related gain for income tax purposes.</p>
<p>The building, called Statesman Park, was sold as part of United Dominion's plan to divest its commercial properties.</p>
</text>
